---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
import profileImage from "../assets/images/joe_laskowski.webp";
import locationImage from "../assets/images/south-bend.webp";

// Career start: 2000. Total years in IT is computed at build time
// so the About page stays current without manual edits each year.
const CAREER_START_YEAR = 2000;
const LINUX_START_YEAR = 2007;
const yearsInIT = new Date().getFullYear() - CAREER_START_YEAR;
const linuxYears = new Date().getFullYear() - LINUX_START_YEAR;
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`About Me | ${SITE_TITLE}`}
  description={`Joe Laskowski — ${yearsInIT} years in IT, currently working in AI, writing here when I've got something worth saying.`}
>
  <div class="container">
    <article class="about-content">
      <div class="hero-section">
        <Image
          src={profileImage}
          alt="Joe Laskowski"
          class="profile-image"
          width={180}
          height={180}
          loading="eager"
        />
        <div class="hero-text">
          <h1 class="gradient-text">About Joe Laskowski</h1>
          <p class="lead">
            {yearsInIT} years in IT, currently working in AI, writing here
            when I've got something worth saying.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="prose">
        <h2 class="accent-blue">The Work</h2>
        <p>
          {yearsInIT} years in IT — the first seventeen at small shops,
          where you ARE the IT department and a printer driver counts as
          a credible cause of death. Nine years in enterprise after that,
          moving through service desk, then service desk lead, then
          Internal IT — where I lived in Microsoft 365, Active Directory,
          Intune, and Entra/Azure (which Microsoft has renamed enough
          times that I've stopped keeping count out of self-respect).
          Long enough, either way, to have watched the same "new"
          framework get rebranded twice and sold back to me. Long enough
          to have strong opinions about why the PowerShell window went
          red at 2 AM.
        </p>

        <p>
          Since April 2026, I've been the AI Quality Analyst at <a
            href="https://www.aunalytics.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Aunalytics</a
          >, a Midwest data platform company. The job, stripped of its
          title, is this: when the AI says something, is it actually right?
          Turns out that's a more interesting question than the marketing
          for any of these systems would have you believe.
        </p>

        <h2 class="accent-green">Building</h2>
        <p>
          Outside the day job there's <a href="https://autoscript.studio" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >AutoScript Studio LLC</a
          > — my Indiana company, and the legal wrapper around the things
          I'm slowly shipping. The brand under it is
          <strong>PixelDrops</strong>, an AI-driven digital-products
          operation: a novel I wrote under a pen name (Amazon launch
          coming), a YouTube channel called <a
            href="https://www.youtube.com/@StackTraceDocs"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer">StackTraceDocs</a
          > — first video is out, and I'm refining the production
          pipeline before the next one — and whatever software ships out
          of the workshop after that. Everything leans hard on AI tooling
          — that's the whole point of doing it now. The blog is where the
          first version of any of it tends to surface.
        </p>

        <h2 class="accent-purple">Off the Clock</h2>
        <p>
          Linux every day for {linuxYears} years — the terminal is where
          I think clearest. A while back I sold my $XLM to buy more $XRP,
          and that's where my crypto attention sits now (it made sense at
          the time; ask me again in five years). The rest of my
          screen-time goes to AI tooling — anything new I can poke at, I
          poke at — the biohacking side of health and longevity, and
          UAPs. The part of the UAP thing I genuinely can't get my head
          around is that every new government disclosure nudges us closer
          to "we are not alone in this universe" and the collective public
          response is, somehow, a shrug. That blows my mind. Most of what
          falls out of any of that ends up on the blog. The rest ends up
          in a drawer.
        </p>

        <p>
          Away from the screen: IPAs of every persuasion (I shop by ABV;
          the higher, the better), hot wings ordered at a heat level my
          friends consider a personal failing, and I'm Star Wars enough to
          keep watching but not enough to fight about it.
        </p>

        <div class="image-section">
          <Image
            src={locationImage}
            alt="South Bend, Indiana"
            class="location-image"
            width={600}
            height={400}
            loading="eager"
          />
          <p class="image-caption">South Bend, Indiana</p>
        </div>

        <h2 class="accent-orange">Family</h2>
        <p>
          Three kids and four grandkids — my two oldest are grown and out
          doing their own thing; AJ, my youngest, is still a kid and is
          with me several days a week. The grandkids are sharper than I
          was at their age and significantly louder. My partner Rianna and
          I started dating on New Year's Day 2025, and between her three
          kids and mine the house is rarely quiet — which, most days, is
          the point.
        </p>

        <p>
          South Bend, Indiana. Real place. Notre Dame, the river, winters
          that make a warm terminal feel like a coping mechanism. I grew
          up here, my kids did too, and I'm not going anywhere.
        </p>

        <h2 class="accent-pink">Let's Connect</h2>
        <p>
          If you want to talk XRP, AI tooling, or whether the UAP stuff
          is finally about to break wide open — social links are in the
          header. The <a href="/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">blog</a>
          is whatever I've been chewing on lately. Or <a href="/contact/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >send me a message</a
          > and we'll go from there.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>

  <style>
    .about-content {
      max-width: 800px;
      margin: 0 auto;
    }

    .hero-section {
      display: flex;
      gap: 3rem;
      align-items: center;
      margin: 3rem 0;
      padding: 2rem 0;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color);
    }

    .profile-image {
      width: 180px;
      height: 180px;
      border-radius: 50%;
      border: 4px solid var(--accent-blue);
      box-shadow: 0 0 20px rgba(0, 212, 255, 0.2);
      flex-shrink: 0;
    }

    .hero-text {
      flex: 1;
    }

    .hero-text h1 {
      font-size: 2.5rem;
      margin: 0 0 1rem 0;
      font-weight: 700;
    }

    .lead {
      font-size: 1.25rem;
      color: var(--text-secondary);
      line-height: 1.6;
      margin: 0;
    }

    .prose {
      margin-top: 3rem;
    }

    .prose h2 {
      font-size: 1.75rem;
      margin: 2.5rem 0 1rem 0;
      font-weight: 600;
    }

    .prose p {
      margin: 1.5rem 0;
      font-size: 1.1rem;
      line-height: 1.7;
    }

    .prose a {
      color: var(--accent-blue);
      font-weight: 600;
      transition:
        color 0.2s ease,
        text-shadow 0.2s ease;
    }

    .prose a:hover {
      color: var(--accent-cyan);
      text-shadow: 0 0 8px rgba(0, 212, 255, 0.3);
      text-decoration: underline;
    }

    .image-section {
      margin: 3rem 0;
      text-align: center;
    }

    .location-image {
      width: 100%;
      max-width: 600px;
      height: auto;
      border-radius: 8px;
      box-shadow: 0 4px 15px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4);
      margin: 0 auto 1rem auto;
      display: block;
    }

    .image-caption {
      font-style: italic;
      color: var(--text-muted);
      margin: 0;
      font-size: 0.95rem;
    }

    @media (max-width: 768px) {
      .hero-section {
        flex-direction: column;
        text-align: center;
        gap: 2rem;
      }

      .hero-text h1 {
        font-size: 2rem;
      }

      .lead {
        font-size: 1.125rem;
      }

      .profile-image {
        width: 150px;
        height: 150px;
      }
    }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
